   "evidence": "QuiverTotal.lean:96-107 has simp lemmas only for `comp_left`, `comp_right` and `mk_comp_mk`, none for `.hom`; Mathlib SingleObj.lean:76 `comp_as_mul` is not @[simp]; the PR's own proof has to unfold `Quiver.Total.comp_def` by hand.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Topology/CategoryTheory/Groupoid/Examples.lean",
   "fix": "Add a `@[simp]` lemma whose left-hand side is `(a.comp b h).hom` (stated through `SingleObj` homs and multiplication) giving `b.hom * a.hom`, or tag `arrowHomeomorph_comp` `@[simp high]` so it fires before `arrowHomeomorph_apply`.",
   "issue": "`arrowHomeomorph_comp` is untagged and its left-hand side is never in simp normal form: `arrowHomeomorph_apply` rewrites it to `(a.comp b h).hom`, which no simp lemma reduces, so `simp` never produces `g * h`.",
   "line": 304
  },
  {
   "evidence": "Mathlib SingleObj.lean:89 `theorem inv_as_inv` carries no simp attribute; Examples.lean `continuous_inverse` calls `simp [SingleObj.inv_as_inv]`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Topology/CategoryTheory/Groupoid/Examples.lean",
   "fix": "Add a `@[simp]` lemma `arrowHomeomorph_inverse` (or one stated through `IsTopologicalGroupoid.inverseHomeomorph`) under `[Group G]` that gives `(arrowHomeomorph G a)\u207b\u00b9`.",
   "issue": "There is no lemma giving the one-object inverse label, `arrowHomeomorph G \u27e8a.right, a.left, inv a.hom\u27e9 = (arrowHomeomorph G a)\u207b\u00b9`. `simp` stops at `inv a.hom` because `SingleObj.inv_as_inv` is not simp, and `continuous_inverse` has to supply it by hand.",
   "line": 329
  }
